  "commentary_text": "The most non-ideal feedback circuit that can be found, is probably the one using a single transistor only. This is a case of severe input loading AND output loading. Everything will interact with everything. It is clear that in this case, the feedback equations can hardly be applied. An attempt is made in this slide. Some approximate expressions are given. The only sure way to obtain an accurate result is to substitute the transistor by its equivalent circuit (with parameters g and r at low frequencies), and solve m o the Kirchoff equations. As a result this is one of the most complicated feedback circuits around, despite its simple circuit configuration.",
